{"full":"hf:danmoreng/macrostories-browser","spaceId":"danmoreng/macrostories-browser","name":"MacroStories Browser Lab","source":"huggingface","description":"A 20K storyteller in your browser. WebGPU + WebAssembly.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"HTML","topics":["static","transformers.js","webgpu","wasm","tiny-language-model","storytelling","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":3,"created":"2026-10-07T17:15:58.000Z","updated":"2026-10-07T17:41:25.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://danmoreng-macrostories-browser.static.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/danmoreng/macrostories-browser","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.403Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.403Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:39.403Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"📖","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser playground for raincandy-u/MacroStories: 19,969 parameters, 378 vocabulary tokens, and one decoder applied four times with shared weights. Inference uses Transformers.js 4.3.1 and ONNX Runtime Web, with WebGPU or WebAssembly in a Web Worker.","The model generates constrained English children's stories. It is a continuation model, so use a story opening rather than an instruction. An empty opening starts generation from its BOS token. Alex, Robin and Casey are display aliases for the model's three person markers.","Features: streaming text, deterministic seed, temperature/greedy mode, top-p, top-k, stop, prompt vocabulary warnings, backend selection, performance statistics, raw output, token IDs, downloadable experiment reports. No prompt or story is sent to an inference server. There is no analytics code, third-party font, or CDN dependency at runtime."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/danmoreng/macrostories-browser/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4ab5afa7f2036ea4fffbd2331ba1626d3cedc80031bdc612da5ae4455d7cd3a3","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T